          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/core"} core
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is the maximal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcategory"} subcategory
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            that is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            and all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphisms"} isomorphisms
            between them. The core is not a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%282%2C1%29-category"} (2,1)-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Cat
                    %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat_g
            of categories, functors, and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphisms"} natural isomorphisms
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coreflective+subcategory"} coreflection
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Cat
                    %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat_g
            into
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gpd"} Gpd
          %p
            In general, for any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            we write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi K
                    %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K_g
            for its “homwise core:” the sub-2-category determined by all the objects and morphisms but only the iso
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-morphisms"} 2-morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi K
                    %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K_g
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%282%2C1%29-category"} (2,1)-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi gpd
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} gpd(K)
            is a full
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sub-2-category"} sub-2-category
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K_g
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+2-category"} regular 2-category
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#core Core
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong core
              of an object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              in a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+2-category"} regular 2-category
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J\to A
              which is
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/eso+morphism"} eso
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudomonic+functor"} pseudomonic
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
              is groupoidal.
          %h3#enough_groupoids Enough groupoids
          %p
            We say that a regular 2-category has
            %strong enough groupoids
            if every object admits an eso from a groupoidal one. Thus, a (2,1)-exact 2-category has cores if and only if it has enough groupoids.
          %p
            Likewise, we say that a regular 2-category has
            %strong enough discretes
            if every object admits an eso from a discrete one. Clearly this is a stronger condition. Note, though, that if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            has enough groupoids, then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi pos
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} pos(K)
            has enough discretes, since the core of any posetal object is discrete.
          %p
            Having enough discretes, or at least enough groupoids, is a very familiar aspect of 2-categories such as
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
            %span.newWikiWord
              internal logic
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/2-internal+logic"} ?
            noticeably easier to work with. However, in a sense none of the really “new” 2-categories have enough groupoids or discretes.
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                The 2-exact 2-categories having enough discretes are precisely the categories of internal categories and anafunctors in 1-exact 1-categories; see
                = succeed "." do
                  %span.newWikiWord
                    exact completion of a 2-category
                    %a{:href => "/nlab/new/exact+completion+of+a+2-category"} ?
            %li
              %p
                Basically the only
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+2-toposes"} Grothendieck 2-toposes
                having enough discretes are the 2-categories of stacks on
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-site"} 1-sites
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#general General
          .num_lemma
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p
              In a regular 2-category
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J\to A
              is a coreflection of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K_g
              into
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi gpd
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} gpd(K)
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              We must show that for any groupoidal
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi gpd
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mi J
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mi J
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} gpd(K)(G,J)=K_g(G,J)\to K_g(G,A)
            %p
              is an equivalence. Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J\to A
              is pseudomonic in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi K
                        %mi g
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K_g
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                      %mo →
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G\to A
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi P
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi J
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi G
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \array{P &amp; \to &amp; J\\ \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow \\ G &amp; \to &amp; A}
            %p
              and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇉
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P_1\;\rightrightarrows\; P
              be the kernel of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                      %mo →
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P\to G
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P\to A
              descends to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              is groupoidal,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇉
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P_1\;\rightrightarrows\; P
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-congruence"} (2,1)-congruence
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                      %mo →
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J\to A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo →
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P\to J
              has an action as well; thus it descends to a map
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                      %mo →
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G\to J
          %p
            In particular, cores in a regular 2-category are unique up to unique equivalence. We write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J(A)
            for the core of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          .num_lemma
            %h6#lemma_2 Lemma
            %p
              An object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              of a (2,1)-exact 2-category has a core if and only if there is an eso
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C\to A
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is groupoidal.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              “Only if” is clear, so suppose that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p:C\to A
              is eso and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is groupoidal. Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mi A
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_1 = C\times_A C
              be the pullback. Then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_1
              is also groupoidal and is a (2,1)-congruence on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi q
                      %mo :
                      %mi C
                      %mo →
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q:C\to J
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                      %mo :
                      %mi J
                      %mo →
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m:J\to A
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %p
              Evidently
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                    %mo :
                    %mi J
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m:J\to A
              is eso, since the eso
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C\to A
              factors through it. And since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_1
              is a (2,1)-congruence, the classification of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-congruence"} congruences
              implies that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
              is groupoidal; thus it remains to show that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
              is pseudomonic.
            %p
              First suppose given
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ,
                      %mi g
                      %mo :
                      %mi X
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ⇉
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f,g: X\;\rightrightarrows\; J
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
              along
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
              gives esos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P_1\to X
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi P
                        %mn 2
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P_2\to X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P = P_1\times_X P_2
              comes with an eso
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo :
                    %mi P
                    %mo →
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r:P \to T
              and two morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo ,
                    %mi k
                    %mo :
                    %mi P
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h,k:P \to C
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                    %mi h
                    %mo ≅
                    %mi f
                    %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q h \cong f r
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi q
                      %mi k
                      %mo ≅
                      %mi g
                      %mi r
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q k \cong g r
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                    %mo ,
                    %mi β
                    %mo :
                    %mi f
                    %mo →
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha,\beta: f\to g
              induce maps
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ⇉
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P\;\rightrightarrows\; C_1
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_1
              is the kernel
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (q/q)
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                      %mi α
                      %mo =
                      %mi m
                      %mi β
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m\alpha = m\beta
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_1
              is also the kernel
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p/p)
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                      %mi r
                      %mo =
                      %mi β
                      %mi r
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha r=\beta r
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
              is eso,
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                      %mo =
                      %mi β
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha=\beta
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
              is faithful.
            %p
              On the other hand, again given
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ,
                      %mi g
                      %mo :
                      %mi X
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ⇉
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f,g: X\;\rightrightarrows\; J
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                    %mo :
                    %mi m
                    %mi f
                    %mo ≅
                    %mi m
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha: m f\cong m g
              induces a map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P\to C_1
              and therefore a 2-cell
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi β
                    %mo :
                    %mi f
                    %mi r
                    %mo →
                    %mi g
                    %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta: f r\to g r
              with
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                      %mi β
                      %mo =
                      %mi α
                      %mi r
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m\beta = \alpha r
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi β
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta
              descends to a 2-cell
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo →
                      %mi g
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\to g
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇉
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P\;\rightrightarrows\; J
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f r
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mi r
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g r
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                    %mi β
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m\beta
              is an action 2-cell, since
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                      %mi β
                      %mo =
                      %mi α
                      %mi r
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m\beta = \alpha r
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
              is faithful, so it reflects the axiom for an action 2-cell. Therefore,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
              is full-on-isomorphisms, and hence pseudomonic.
          %h3#subobjects Subobjects
          %p
            We also remark that cores, when they exist, “capture all the information about
            = succeed ".\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobjects"} subobjects
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              is a regular 2-category and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is an object having a core
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                      %mo :
                      %mi J
                      %mo →
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j:J\to A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi j
                      %mo *
                    %mo :
                    %mi Sub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Sub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi J
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j^*:Sub(A)\to Sub(J)
              is an equivalence.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              It is a general fact in a regular 2-category that for any eso
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:X\to Y
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo :
                    %mi Sub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Sub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*:Sub(Y)\to Sub(X)
              is full (and faithful, which of course is automatic for a functor between posets). For if
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %mi U
                      %mo ≤
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*U \le f^*V
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi f
                              %mo *
                            %mi U
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi f
                              %mo *
                            %mi V
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi V
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi U
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{f^*U &amp; \to &amp; f^*V &amp; \to &amp; V\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp;&amp;&amp; \downarrow\\
                    U &amp; &amp; \to &amp; &amp; Y}
            %p
              in which
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mi U
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*U \to U
              is eso and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V\to Y
              is ff, hence we have
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo →
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\to V
              over
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            %p
              Thus, in our case,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi j
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j^*
              is full and faithful since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
              is eso, so it suffices to show that for any ff
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo →
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\to J
              we have
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi j
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mo ∃
                      %mi j
                    %mi U
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j^* \exists_j U \le U
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Sub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi J
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sub(J)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi U
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ∃
                              %mi j
                            %mi U
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi J
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{U &amp; \to &amp; \exists_j U\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow\\
                    J &amp; \to &amp; X}
            %p
              where the vertical arrows are ff and the bottom arrow
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J\to X
              is faithful and pseudomonic, from which it follows that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mo ∃
                      %mi j
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\to \exists_j U
              is also faithful and pseudomonic. Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mo ∃
                      %mi j
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\to \exists_j U
              is eso by definition,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              is a core of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo ∃
                        %mi j
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exists_j U
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi j
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mo ∃
                      %mi j
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j^*\exists_j U
              is a groupoid mapping to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
